Section 1 (Purpose)
This license lets anyone freely use, modify, and distribute Kkomi Note
("the Software") for noncommercial purposes, while ensuring that modified
versions are also distributed free of charge together with their source.

Section 2 (Definitions)
1. "The Software" means the source code, documentation, and executables
   published in the original repository, and anything derived from them.
2. "Modified Version" means any software made by changing, combining, or
   building on all or part of the Software.
3. "Distribute" means giving copies of the Software or a Modified Version
   to others, making them available for download, or making them available
   for others to use over a network.
4. "Commercial Purpose" means obtaining monetary compensation or commercial
   advantage from the Software or a Modified Version, including but not
   limited to:
   a. selling, or distributing for a fee, the Software or a Modified
      Version;
   b. including or bundling the Software or a Modified Version in a paid
      product, paid service, or paid subscription;
   c. charging fees, earning advertising revenue, or imposing membership
      or other consideration for using the Software or a Modified Version.
5. The following are not Commercial Purposes:
   a. use by teachers, instructors, or school staff for student
      management, teaching, or their work (allowed even if their employer
      is a for-profit organization, as long as no compensation is received
      for the Software itself);
   b. use by schools, education offices, research institutions, or
      nonprofit organizations;
   c. personal study, research, or testing;
   d. introducing the Software or explaining how to use it in training,
      lectures, or classes, including paid training or lectures for which
      the instructor receives a fee (selling or distributing the Software
      or a Modified Version itself for a fee is still not allowed).

Section 3 (Grant)
Provided you comply with this license, anyone may use, copy, modify, and
distribute the Software free of charge for noncommercial purposes.

Section 4 (No Commercial Purpose)
The Software and any Modified Version may not be used or distributed for a
Commercial Purpose.

Section 5 (Free Distribution)
You may not charge any fee when distributing the Software or a Modified
Version.

Section 6 (Source Disclosure for Modified Versions)
Anyone who distributes a Modified Version must:
1. publish the complete source code of the Modified Version where anyone
   can obtain it free of charge;
2. apply this license unchanged to the whole Modified Version and include
   the full text of this license, without adding further conditions or
   reducing any rights;
3. when distributing only executables, clearly state in the same place
   where the source can be obtained.

Section 7 (Notices)
1. You must keep the copyright notice (Copyright (c) 2026 purnpado) and
   the original repository address.
2. A Modified Version must clearly state that it has been modified and by
   whom.
3. A Modified Version must not be presented as an official release by the
   original author.

Section 8 (No Warranty; Limitation of Liability)
The Software is provided "as is". The original author makes no warranty of
any kind, including fitness for a particular purpose, absence of errors, or
the safety of data. To the extent permitted by law, the original author is
not liable for any data loss, personal data breach, or any other damage
arising from the use of the Software. Users are responsible for backing up
and protecting student data.

Section 9 (Termination)
Your rights under this license end automatically if you violate it.
However, they are reinstated if you cure the violation within 30 days after
first receiving notice of it from the original author.

Section 10 (Separate Permission)
The original author may grant permission to use the Software under terms
different from this license. For commercial use inquiries, feedback, or
bug reports, please open an issue in the original repository
(https://github.com/purnpado/komi_note/issues).

Section 11 (Interpretation)
This license is governed by the laws of the Republic of Korea. If the
Korean and English texts differ, the Korean text prevails.
